# Fallback public entry point for the BFF — docs/15-launch-checklist.md, option B.
#
# This file is only served when the `caddy` compose profile is enabled, which
# ./stack/wa does when CADDY_API_HOST is set in stack/.env (empty by default).
# That deliberately opens inbound 80 and 443 on the VM — the one documented
# exception to the zero-inbound-port rule — so it needs the owner's approval.
# Option A (Cloudflare for SaaS through the tunnel) opens no port and is the
# default path; reach for this file only if option A cannot be used.
#
# Caddy substitutes {$CADDY_API_HOST} from the container's environment at parse
# time (docker compose passes it through in stack/compose.infra.yml). Caddy then
# issues a real Let's Encrypt certificate for exactly that hostname, over
# the ports published in stack/compose.infra.yml, and proxies to the BFF on the
# compose network. An empty value leaves the site block empty and Caddy refuses
# to start, which is the intended loud failure.
{$CADDY_API_HOST} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy openwa-bff:4000
}
